  "implemented": [
    "Textarea selectionStart, selectionEnd, selectionDirection, setSelectionRange and select use source argument conversions.",
    "The cache and focused FrameSelection are separate. The model records editor revision and directionality.",
    "Focus with preventScroll restores the cache before synchronous source focus callbacks. Select restores it after the focus procedure.",
    "Changed cached ranges queue trusted bubbling select events. The animation stage freezes its FIFO before dispatch.",
    "Changed represented frame ranges queue separate trusted nonbubbling Document selectionchange tasks. Neither event class is coalesced.",
    "Callbacks run through the source interpreter. The dispatch path uses current listeners and retains detached event targets.",
    "The positive textarea focus-style query checks native layout-object existence and inherited visibility without a measured rectangle."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "The rendering cadence and ordering among native task sources are explicit environment requirements. Diagnostics supply event stages; they do not establish a cadence.",
    "Default focus scrolling remains unresolved. Readonly alone is not a proof that scrolling has no effect.",
    "Editing, arbitrary document selections, and mutations that require native frame-range adjustment remain unresolved.",
    "The source wrapper admits no policy or completion boundary inside an active rendering batch, native event dispatch, focus procedure or selectionchange task.",
    "The comparison results do not prove full native refinement or an optimal full-game strategy."
  ],
